&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow a team of engineers, fostering a culture of trust, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own team execution and delivery: roadmap planning, goal setting, and shipping well-tested, usable products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure adherence to engineering best practices, including quality, observability, testing, security, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build partnerships across Product, Data, and Ops to align on priorities and drive business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop team members through mentorship, coaching, and thoughtful career conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to org-wide engineering practices: on-call readiness, DORA metrics, onboarding, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a software engineer working on distributed systems in Python, Java, Kotlin, Go, or JavaScript/TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing engineers, ideally on small, fast-moving squads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication, a bias toward action, and the ability to navigate ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building resilient systems and leading teams through scaling challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in our stack or learning quickly: Java/Python/Go, React, Postgres, AWS, Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
